PSSS — Particle Systems Screen Saver
====================================

This repository contains a modified and substantially extended version of PSSS.


The original work
-----------------

PSSS — Particle Systems Screen Saver — was created by Andreas Kardin, who
publishes as *mephzara*: the idea, the name, the mathematics and the original
implementation are his.

    Original source   https://github.com/mephzara/psss_js
    Original demo     http://mephzara.com/misc/psss_js/

`psss-original/` holds that JavaScript implementation as it stood when the
TypeScript rewrite began, together with its own copy of the licence. It is kept
read-only and is never edited by the work in `psss-engine/`.

It is a SNAPSHOT rather than a copy of the upstream tip, and the difference is
stated here rather than left for a reader to discover. `LICENSE` and
`psss_presets.json` are byte-identical to the original; `psss.js` (1591 -> 5078
lines) and `index.html` (622 -> 1070 lines) carry substantial further work done
on the JavaScript version in this project before the rewrite began.

The sharing has not been one-directional, so a difference between this snapshot
and the upstream repository is not evidence of a single direction of copying:
this extended JavaScript demo was shared with the original author, and the
upstream repository may since have taken parts of it up. The upstream repository
linked above is the author's own current state and is the place to look for it.


Modifications
-------------

This version adds a second, independent implementation of PSSS in
`psss-engine/` — TypeScript and WebGL2 in place of JavaScript and a 2D canvas —
together with a preset library, a control surface, a Windows screensaver host
and the two reference documents in the repository root.

    Modifications copyright (C) 2025-2026 Rico Cozzio

The preset format of the original is preserved, so an original preset still
loads. `psss-original/` is frozen: nothing in `psss-engine/` writes to it, and
no further change is made to it.


